window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-d8c21044e817c0d5"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"roll-out-a-gateway\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">部署网关</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>通过网关部署 API/提供商凭据访问路径。配置模型路由、签发开发者凭据，并分发经过验证的 Codex 配置。如果要转发 ChatGPT 工作区请求，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-e25dfff3918fe597\">通过网关使用 ChatGPT 登录</a>。</p> <p>如果要在自己的计算机上使用已获得的信息配置 Codex，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">使用 API/提供商凭据</a>。选择或部署网关之前，请先阅读<a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">网关兼容性要求</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"prerequisites\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">前提条件</h2> <p>向开发者部署 Codex 前，请确认已准备好以下内容：</p> <ul> <li>一个通过 HTTPS 提供服务、且基础 URL 与计划分发的 URL 完全一致的网关。</li> <li>保存在网关上的上游提供商凭据。</li> <li>已批准并映射到预期上游模型的 Codex 模型别名。</li> <li>具有限定作用域的网关测试凭据。</li> <li>机密信息分发机制或经过测试的凭据助手。</li> <li>分发配置、助手可执行文件和目录文件的方式。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"gateway-requirements\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">网关要求</h2> <p>连接 Codex 前，请验证网关产品保留了以下必需行为：</p> <ul> <li>接受发送到 <code>POST /v1/responses</code> 的 Codex Responses API 请求。</li> <li>不经缓冲地流式传输 SSE 事件，并以 <code>response.completed</code> 结束。</li> <li>支持通过重放输入继续进行后续对话轮次。</li> <li>仅在启用 WebSocket 或增量传输时保留 <code>previous_response_id</code>。</li> <li>保留函数调用及与之匹配的 <code>function_call_output</code> 项。</li> <li>将每个面向 Codex 的模型别名路由到预期上游模型。</li> <li>分别验证用户身份，并返回有助于排障且不隐去原因的错误信息。</li> </ul> <p>仅有健康检查端点、<code>/v1/models</code>、Chat Completions 响应或一条纯文本回复，并不足以证明网关符合要求。详细约定请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">网关兼容性要求</a>。</p> <p>需要实现示例作为起点？<a href=\"https://github.com/openai-on-aws/guidance-codex/tree/adbc00f353effbf0252e667ba41eb89c99324c8f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex 部署指南代码库（需联网）</a>包含多种 LLM 网关产品的配置示例。请先确认网关符合上述要求，再将它作为参考。</p> <p><a id=\"roll-out-the-gateway\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">部署网关</h2> <p>要从网关部署转向经过验证的开发者使用体验，请按顺序完成以下五个检查点：</p> <ol> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=choose-model-names-and-routes\">选择模型名称并验证路由</a>。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=issue-developer-credentials\">签发开发者凭据</a>。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=test-the-client-and-gateway\">通过网关测试 Codex</a>。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=distribute-the-configuration\">分发配置</a>。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=verify-and-operate-the-rollout\">在开发者计算机上验证</a>。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"choose-model-names-and-routes\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">选择模型名称并配置路由</h2> <p>将 Codex 的 <code>model</code> 设置为网关模型名称。配置网关，将该名称路由到已批准的上游模型。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>网关模型名称</th> <th>Codex 配置</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>你的 Codex 版本中包含的<a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26?anchor=recognized-model-names\">内置模型名称</a></td> <td>在 <code>config.toml</code> 中将 <code>model</code> 设置为此确切名称。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>自定义别名，例如 <code>company-coding-model</code></td> <td>提供包含该别名及对应模型元数据的远程或本地目录。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"supply-metadata-for-a-custom-alias\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"use-a-model-catalog-for-custom-names\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">为自定义名称使用模型目录</h3> <p>如果网关使用 Codex 无法识别的模型名称，请提供模型目录。目录会提供 Codex 对该名称使用的指令、推理选项、上下文限制和工具能力。若没有匹配条目，请求虽然可能到达预期上游模型，但 Codex 会使用通用设置。</p> <p>可通过 <code>model_providers.&lt;id&gt;.model_catalog_url</code> 托管远程目录，以集中更新模型元数据；也可使用 <code>model_catalog_json</code> 分发本地文件。两个设置的详情请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">配置参考</a>。</p> <p>例如，将 <code>company-coding-model</code> 用作 <code>gpt-6-luna</code> 的别名：</p> <ol> <li>在网关中创建 <code>company-coding-model</code> 别名，并将其路由到已批准的上游 <code>gpt-6-luna</code> 模型。</li> <li>下载与你的 Codex 版本相匹配的 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex 模型目录（需联网）</a>，并将副本保存为 <code>gateway-models.json</code>。以此文件为基础进行修改。</li> <li>编辑副本中的 <code>gpt-6-luna</code> 条目：将 <code>slug</code> 设为 <code>company-coding-model</code>，并检查其余元数据是否与上游模型和网关能力相匹配。若该别名不涉及模型迁移，请将 <code>upgrade</code> 设为 <code>null</code>。</li> <li>保留顶层 <code>models</code> 数组中的条目。加入用户需要选择的所有模型，然后按下文所述通过目录端点提供该文件，或在本地分发。</li> </ol> <p>若要为特定 Codex 版本使用目录，请运行 <code>codex --version</code> 并选择匹配的 <code>rust-v&lt;version&gt;</code> 标签。对于自定义构建，请使用其准确的源代码提交。对于桌面应用部署，请匹配其捆绑的 CLI 版本。</p> <p>通过 LiteLLM 使用 Bedrock 时，请应用<a href=\"#/article/a-886686d95c8255a4?anchor=prepare-the-client-catalog\">必需的目录修改</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"serve-a-remote-catalog\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_7\">提供远程目录</h4> <p>通过 HTTPS 端点直接返回准备好的 <code>gateway-models.json</code> 文件内容。将完整端点 URL 分发到所选提供商的 <code>config.toml</code> 表中：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model = \"company-coding-model\"\nmodel_provider = \"enterprise-gateway\"\nweb_search = \"disabled\"\n\n[model_providers.enterprise-gateway]\nname = \"Organization Gateway\"\nbase_url = \"https://gateway.example.com/v1\"\nmodel_catalog_url = \"https://gateway.example.com/codex/models.json\"\nwire_api = \"responses\"\nenv_key = \"CODEX_GATEWAY_API_KEY\"\n</code></pre> <p>确保 Codex 进程能够读取 <code>CODEX_GATEWAY_API_KEY</code>。请单独设置 <code>base_url</code>，以便通过网关路由推理请求。如果省略此设置，Codex 会根据当前身份验证模式使用默认 OpenAI 端点。</p> <p>目录发现要求使用 API 密钥、基于命令的身份验证或 Codex 后端身份验证。仅使用自定义标头不会触发目录发现。</p> <p>目录端点必须满足以下要求：</p> <ul> <li>接受对已配置 URL 发起的 <code>GET</code> 请求，包括 Codex 添加的 <code>client_version</code> 查询参数，以及任何已配置的提供商 <code>query_params</code>。</li> <li>接受所选提供商的身份验证和已配置标头。目录应托管在获准接收这些凭据的服务上。</li> <li>返回顶层 <code>models</code> 数组，其中包含与客户端版本匹配的完整 Codex 模型元数据。应使用上文准备的版本匹配目录，而不是只返回模型 ID 列表。每个条目都必须具有唯一且非空的 <code>slug</code>。</li> <li>直接返回 JSON，不要重定向；响应大小不得超过 1 MiB。</li> </ul> <p>获准模型发生变化时，请更新目录。更改配置后重新启动客户端。</p> <p>请移除任何当前生效的 <code>model_catalog_json</code> 设置，包括通过 <code>requirements.toml</code> 强制执行的设置。该设置优先级高于远程 URL，并会阻止获取远程目录。</p> <p><a id=\"distribute-a-local-catalog\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_8\">分发本地目录</h4> <p>使用 <code>model_catalog_json</code> 在启动时加载准备好的文件。本地自定义目录会替换随程序捆绑的目录。</p> <p>将网关别名、目录 <code>slug</code> 和 Codex <code>model</code> 均设为 <code>company-coding-model</code>。在要分发的 Codex 配置中，将这些设置放在第一个 TOML 表之前，并使用文件的实际绝对路径：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model = \"company-coding-model\"\nmodel_catalog_json = \"/absolute/path/to/gateway-models.json\"\n</code></pre> <p>更改目录后，请重新启动 CLI 或桌面应用，因为 Codex 会在启动时加载目录。</p> <p><a id=\"verify-model-routes\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">验证模型路由</h3> <p>对于每个模型，请通过真实的 Responses 请求和网关记录验证路由。<code>/v1/models</code> 响应有助于发现模型名称，但不能证明模型支持所需请求和工具行为。</p> <p>模型路由和工具授权是部署中的不同部分。请分别配置 MCP 连接、插件分发及其策略。</p> <p><a id=\"issue-developer-credentials\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">签发开发者凭据</h2> <ol> <li>为每位开发者签发一个具有限定作用域的网关凭据，以便分别归因使用情况并单独撤销访问权限。</li> <li>为每个凭据设置获准模型、速率限制、预算、到期时间和续期周期。</li> <li>通过机密管理器或已安装的凭据助手分发凭据。不要将上游提供商凭据和网关管理员凭据放在开发者计算机上。</li> <li>如果使用凭据助手，请遵循 <a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85?anchor=custom-model-providers\">基于命令的身份验证约定</a> 约定，并在分发前测试令牌获取和刷新。</li> <li>告知开发者如何续期凭据，以及遇到问题时应联系谁。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"test-the-client-and-gateway\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"test-codex-through-the-gateway\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex\">通过网关测试 Codex</h2> <p>分发任何配置前，请按照<a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">使用 API/提供商凭据</a>操作，为一位隔离的测试用户配置计划分发的提供商配置块和凭据机制。</p> <p>请从开发者将要使用的同一 CLI 或桌面界面运行以下检查：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>检查项</th> <th>操作</th> <th>通过标准</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>连接</td> <td>按照<a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694?anchor=verify-the-connection\">验证连接</a>操作。</td> <td>预期提供商和别名处于启用状态，测试提示成功，并且网关日志能识别测试用户。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>流式输出</td> <td>要求生成一段包含多个段落的简短回答。</td> <td>网关不经缓冲地转发 SSE 事件，文本逐步到达，并以 <code>response.completed</code> 结束。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>本地工具调用</td> <td>在具有只读权限的一次性文件夹中，让 Codex 列出顶层文件并进行概述。</td> <td>Codex 发起本地工具调用、返回结果，并在不进行编辑的情况下生成最终回答。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>后续对话</td> <td>在同一对话中提出后续问题。</td> <td>回答会结合上一轮内容；网关接受重放的输入。如果启用了 WebSocket 或增量传输，还会保留 <code>previous_response_id</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>错误处理和归因</td> <td>使用故意无效的测试别名或过期测试凭据重复测试。</td> <td>客户端收到有用的路由或身份验证错误，且有效请求仍能归因到测试用户。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>这些检查均通过后，请开发者按照<a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">使用 API/提供商凭据</a>为自己的计算机进行配置和验证。</p> <p><a id=\"distribute-the-configuration\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">分发配置</h2> <p>为了让所有计算机使用相同的连接路径，请分发网关基础 URL、提供商 ID、获准模型别名和凭据机制。</p> <p><a id=\"what-to-distribute\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_12\">分发哪些内容</h3> <p>要设置提供商默认值，请通过所选配置层分发此 <code>config.toml</code> 配置块。使用当前 Codex 版本能够识别的模型，或提供上文所述的匹配目录。请将令牌解析程序安装到所配置的命令路径：</p> <p>将 <code>model</code> 和 <code>model_provider</code> 放在第一个 TOML 表之前。如果设置了 <code>model_catalog_json</code>，也应将它放在那里。TOML 会把 <code>[model_providers...]</code> 之后的键视为该表的内容，而不是 Codex 顶层配置。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model = \"gpt-6-sol\"\nmodel_provider = \"enterprise-gateway\"\nweb_search = \"disabled\"\n\n[model_providers.enterprise-gateway]\nname = \"Organization Gateway\"\nbase_url = \"https://gateway.example.com/v1\"\nwire_api = \"responses\"\n\n[model_providers.enterprise-gateway.auth]\ncommand = \"/usr/local/bin/fetch-codex-gateway-token\"\nargs = [\"print-token\"]\ntimeout_ms = 30000\nrefresh_interval_ms = 300000\n</code></pre> <p>对于短期静态测试密钥，请移除身份验证配置块，并在 <code>[model_providers.enterprise-gateway]</code> 中设置 <code>env_key = \"CODEX_GATEWAY_API_KEY\"</code>；该变量应在 TOML 之外设置。不要将 <code>env_key</code> 与基于命令的身份验证同时配置。</p> <p><a id=\"distribute-defaults-and-requirements\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_13\">分发默认值和强制要求</h3> <p>请根据<a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76?anchor=configuration-precedence\">配置优先级</a>选择分发默认值的位置。有关强制设置和 macOS MDM 配置描述文件，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=admin-enforced-requirements-requirementstoml\">托管配置</a>。</p> <p>macOS 或 Linux 的主机级默认配置请使用 <code>/etc/codex/config.toml</code>。Windows 上请将 <code>config.toml</code> 放在 <code>%ProgramData%\\OpenAI\\Codex\\</code>。用户和配置文件可以覆盖这些默认值。上述参考资料说明了支持的强制要求及其文件位置。</p> <p>引用的助手可执行文件和本地目录文件都需要单独分发。</p> <p>若要强制使用远程目录 URL，请在 <code>requirements.toml</code> 的 <code>[model_providers.&lt;id&gt;]</code> 下放入完整提供商定义。强制执行的提供商定义会替换普通配置中的匹配提供商表；请在其中包含 <code>base_url</code>、身份验证设置和其他必需字段。如果还要强制指定提供商选择，请使用 <code>model_provider</code> 强制要求。</p> <p><code>model_catalog_json</code> 指向本地 JSON 文件。如果通过 <code>requirements.toml</code> 强制执行此设置，该强制要求只会固定文件路径，不会分发文件。请在 Codex 启动前将目录文件放到该绝对路径下。</p> <p>请在 TOML 中填写已解析的 Windows 绝对路径。Codex 不会展开 <code>model_catalog_json</code> 或提供商身份验证 <code>command</code> 值中的 <code>%ProgramData%</code>。例如，仅当部署确实将文件放在下列路径时才使用这些路径：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model_catalog_json = 'C:\\ProgramData\\OpenAI\\Codex\\models.json'\n\n[model_providers.enterprise-gateway.auth]\ncommand = 'C:\\ProgramData\\OpenAI\\Codex\\fetch-gateway-token.cmd'\nargs = [\"print-token\"]\n</code></pre> <p>WSL 中的 CLI 会读取 Linux 路径和 Linux <code>CODEX_HOME</code>；它不会自动继承 Windows 原生配置。</p> <p><a id=\"hand-developers-the-configuration-values\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_14\">向开发者提供配置值</h3> <p>如果没有托管分发方式，请向每位开发者提供网关 URL、提供商 ID、模型别名、凭据变量或解析程序，以及目录 URL 或本地路径。请他们按照<a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">使用 API/提供商凭据</a>配置并验证自己的计算机。</p> <p>手动设置不属于强制执行渠道。项目本地的 <code>.codex/config.toml</code> 无法覆盖敏感的提供商或身份验证路由键。</p> <p><a id=\"verify-and-operate-the-rollout\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"verify-from-a-developer-machine\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_15\">在开发者计算机上验证</h2> <p>请按以下步骤确认分发的设置已到达开发者计算机：</p> <ol> <li>重新启动 Codex，并确认预期的提供商和模型。</li> <li>按照<a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694?anchor=verify-the-connection\">使用 API/提供商凭据</a>中的简短测试进行验证。</li> <li>提出一个后续问题以确认对话可以继续，然后在网关日志中检查该开发者的请求。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"troubleshoot-rollout-failures\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_16\">排查部署问题</h3> <p>根据问题定位需要检查的配置、凭据或网关层：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>问题</th> <th>处理方法</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>重启后找不到预期提供商。</td> <td>检查当前生效的配置层。用户或配置文件设置可能会覆盖系统默认值。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>所有用户都无法通过身份验证。</td> <td>检查网关身份验证和上游提供商凭据；确认是哪个服务拒绝了请求。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>只有一位用户无法通过身份验证。</td> <td>检查该用户的网关凭据或令牌解析程序。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>流式输出停滞。</td> <td>检查网关缓冲情况以及是否转发了终止事件 <code>response.completed</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>找不到模型或模型能力为通用配置。</td> <td>如果使用自定义别名，请确认网关别名、Codex <code>model</code> 和目录 <code>slug</code> 相互匹配。检查<a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=use-a-model-catalog-for-custom-names\">目录</a>路径及其与已安装 Codex 版本的兼容性，然后重新启动 Codex。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Windows 路径无效。</td> <td>使用已解析的绝对路径。在 TOML 中，Windows 路径应使用单引号字符串和单个反斜杠。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"reuse-an-existing-gateway-deployment\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_17\">复用现有网关部署</h2> <p>如果组织已经通过网关使用 Claude Code，可能可以复用网关产品、网络路径、日志和 Bedrock 访问。保留当前正常运行的设置，同时新增面向 Codex 的 Responses 路由、凭据、模型别名和 <code>config.toml</code>。Claude 客户端设置和 <code>/v1/messages</code> 约定不能用于配置 Codex。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>现有 Claude 部署</th> <th>迁移到 Codex</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>网关产品、DNS、TLS、私有网络、日志、脱敏和监控</td> <td>保留这些服务。新增符合<a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">网关兼容性要求</a>的 Codex 路由。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Bedrock 账户、提供商凭据、IAM 边界、推理配置文件和凭据轮换</td> <td>只有在它们能够授权新 Codex 别名背后的上游模型时才保留。提供商凭据仍保存在网关上。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Claude <code>/v1/messages</code> 路由、Bedrock InvokeModel 请求格式、Anthropic 标头以及 Claude 专用重试或错误处理</td> <td>不要将这些作为兼容性证明。Codex 需要 <code>POST /v1/responses</code>、Responses 流式输出、对话继续、工具调用和有用的错误信息。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN</code>、<code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code> 或 <code>apiKeyHelper</code></td> <td>Codex 不支持 <code>apiKeyHelper</code>。请签发具有限定作用域的 Codex 网关凭据，并通过 <code>env_key</code> 或 Codex 基于命令的令牌解析程序进行配置。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Claude 模型名称、<code>ANTHROPIC_MODEL</code>、<code>ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_*_MODEL</code>、<code>modelOverrides</code> 和 Bedrock 配置文件映射</td> <td>请网关团队<a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=choose-model-names-and-routes\">选择模型名称并配置所需自定义别名</a>。使用他们提供的模型名称以及<a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">模型目录 JSON</a>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Claude <code>settings.json</code>、<code>managed-settings.json</code>、JSON <code>env</code> 块、<code>plist</code> 或注册表配置</td> <td>保留现有 MDM 或配置管理渠道，但改为分发 Codex <code>config.toml</code> 和受支持的 <code>requirements.toml</code> 值。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>为安全迁移，请按顺序完成以下步骤：</p> <ol> <li>盘点当前 Claude 路径：网关 URL、凭据来源、必需标头、模型别名、Bedrock 配置文件映射和托管分发渠道。</li> <li>新增一条并行的 Codex Responses 路由和 Codex 模型别名。</li> <li>签发一个具有限定作用域的 Codex 凭据。如果 Codex 使用静态凭据，请通过 <code>env_key</code> 提供新凭据；如果 Claude 使用凭据助手，请实现并测试 Codex 基于命令的令牌解析约定。</li> <li>使用<a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=what-to-distribute\">提供商配置块</a>配置开发者。对于托管部署，请根据<a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=distribute-the-configuration\">网关部署</a>中说明的 Codex 路径和优先级调整配置描述文件。</li> <li>在开发者实际使用的 CLI 或桌面界面上执行简短连接检查，然后按照<a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=test-the-client-and-gateway\">通过网关测试 Codex</a>执行完整的流式输出、对话继续、工具调用、错误、日志和别名路由检查。</li> <li>试点通过后，向其余开发者<a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=distribute-the-configuration\">分发配置</a>。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"related-docs\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_18\">相关文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">使用 API/提供商凭据</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">托管配置</a></li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"roll-out-a-gateway\">Roll out a gateway</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Roll out the API/provider credential path through your gateway. Configure model routes, issue developer credentials, and distribute a verified Codex configuration. For a gateway that forwards ChatGPT workspace requests, see <a href=\"#/article/a-e25dfff3918fe597\">Sign in with ChatGPT through a gateway</a>.</p> <p>To configure Codex on your own machine with values you were given, see <a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">Use API/provider credentials</a>. Before choosing or rolling out a gateway, review the <a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">gateway compatibility requirements</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"prerequisites\">Prerequisites</h2> <p>Before deploying Codex to developers, confirm that you have:</p> <ul> <li>A gateway serving HTTPS at the exact base URL you will distribute.</li> <li>An upstream provider credential held by the gateway.</li> <li>Approved Codex-facing model aliases mapped to intended upstream models.</li> <li>A scoped test gateway credential.</li> <li>A secret delivery mechanism or a tested credential helper.</li> <li>A way to distribute configuration, helper executables, and any catalog files.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"gateway-requirements\">Gateway requirements</h2> <p>Before connecting Codex, verify that the gateway product preserves these required behaviors:</p> <ul> <li>Accept Codex Responses API requests at <code>POST /v1/responses</code>.</li> <li>Stream SSE events without buffering and end with <code>response.completed</code>.</li> <li>Preserve follow-up continuation with replayed input.</li> <li>Preserve <code>previous_response_id</code> only when WebSocket or incremental transport is enabled.</li> <li>Preserve function calls and matching <code>function_call_output</code> items.</li> <li>Route each Codex-facing model alias to the intended upstream model.</li> <li>Authenticate users separately and return useful errors without hiding the cause.</li> </ul> <p>A health endpoint, <code>/v1/models</code>, Chat Completions response, or one plain-text reply does not qualify the gateway. See <a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">Gateway compatibility requirements</a> for the detailed contract.</p> <p>Need an implementation starting point? The <a href=\"https://github.com/openai-on-aws/guidance-codex/tree/adbc00f353effbf0252e667ba41eb89c99324c8f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex deployment guidance repository (online)</a> includes worked setups for different LLM gateway products. Use it as a reference after confirming your gateway meets the requirements above.</p> <h2 id=\"roll-out-the-gateway\">Roll out the gateway</h2> <p>To move from a deployed gateway to a verified developer experience, complete these five checkpoints in order:</p> <ol> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=choose-model-names-and-routes\">Choose model names and verify routes</a>.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=issue-developer-credentials\">Issue developer credentials</a>.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=test-the-client-and-gateway\">Test Codex through the gateway</a>.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=distribute-the-configuration\">Distribute the configuration</a>.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=verify-and-operate-the-rollout\">Verify from a developer machine</a>.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"choose-model-names-and-routes\">Choose model names and routes</h2> <p>Set Codex's <code>model</code> to the gateway's model name. Configure the gateway to route that name to the approved upstream model.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Gateway model name</th> <th>Codex configuration</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>A <a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26?anchor=recognized-model-names\">built-in model name</a> included in your Codex version</td> <td>Set <code>model</code> in <code>config.toml</code> to this exact name.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>A custom alias, such as <code>company-coding-model</code></td> <td>Supply a remote or local catalog containing the alias and the corresponding model's metadata.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"supply-metadata-for-a-custom-alias\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"use-a-model-catalog-for-custom-names\">Use a model catalog for custom names</h3> <p>Supply a model catalog when your gateway uses a model name Codex does not recognize. The catalog supplies the instructions, reasoning options, context limits, and tool capabilities Codex uses for that name. Without a matching entry, a request can reach the intended upstream model while Codex uses generic settings.</p> <p>Host a remote catalog with <code>model_providers.&lt;id&gt;.model_catalog_url</code> to update model metadata centrally, or distribute a local file with <code>model_catalog_json</code>. See the <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">configuration reference</a> for both settings.</p> <p>For example, to use <code>company-coding-model</code> as an alias for <code>gpt-6-luna</code>:</p> <ol> <li>Create the <code>company-coding-model</code> alias on the gateway and route it to the approved upstream <code>gpt-6-luna</code> model.</li> <li>Download the <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex model catalog (online)</a> for your Codex version and save a copy as <code>gateway-models.json</code>. Use this file as your starting point.</li> <li>Edit the <code>gpt-6-luna</code> entry in your copy: set <code>slug</code> to <code>company-coding-model</code> and check that the remaining metadata matches the upstream model and gateway capabilities. For an alias without a model migration, set <code>upgrade</code> to <code>null</code>.</li> <li>Keep the entries in the top-level <code>models</code> array. Include every model users need to select, then serve the file from a catalog endpoint or distribute it locally as described below.</li> </ol> <p>To use a catalog for a specific Codex version, check <code>codex --version</code> and select the matching <code>rust-v&lt;version&gt;</code> tag. For a custom build, use its exact source commit. For a desktop deployment, match the bundled CLI version.</p> <p>For Bedrock through LiteLLM, apply the <a href=\"#/article/a-886686d95c8255a4?anchor=prepare-the-client-catalog\">required catalog edits</a>.</p> <h4 id=\"serve-a-remote-catalog\">Serve a remote catalog</h4> <p>Serve the prepared <code>gateway-models.json</code> as the response body of an HTTPS endpoint. Distribute the full endpoint URL in the selected provider's <code>config.toml</code> table:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model = \"company-coding-model\"\nmodel_provider = \"enterprise-gateway\"\nweb_search = \"disabled\"\n\n[model_providers.enterprise-gateway]\nname = \"Organization Gateway\"\nbase_url = \"https://gateway.example.com/v1\"\nmodel_catalog_url = \"https://gateway.example.com/codex/models.json\"\nwire_api = \"responses\"\nenv_key = \"CODEX_GATEWAY_API_KEY\"\n</code></pre> <p>Make <code>CODEX_GATEWAY_API_KEY</code> available to the Codex process. Set <code>base_url</code> separately to route inference through the gateway. If you omit it, Codex uses the default OpenAI endpoint for the current authentication mode.</p> <p>Discovery requires API-key, command-backed, or Codex-backend authentication. Custom headers alone don't trigger it.</p> <p>The catalog endpoint must:</p> <ul> <li>Accept <code>GET</code> requests at the configured URL, including the <code>client_version</code> query parameter Codex adds and any configured provider <code>query_params</code>.</li> <li>Accept the selected provider's authentication and configured headers. Host the catalog on a service authorized to receive those credentials.</li> <li>Return a top-level <code>models</code> array with complete Codex model metadata matching the client's version. Use the version-matched catalog prepared above, rather than a list of model IDs. Give each entry a unique, nonempty <code>slug</code>.</li> <li>Return the JSON directly without redirects and keep the response within 1 MiB.</li> </ul> <p>Update the catalog when your approved models change. Restart the client after changing its configuration.</p> <p>Remove any effective <code>model_catalog_json</code> setting, including one enforced through <code>requirements.toml</code>. It takes precedence over the remote URL and prevents fetching.</p> <h4 id=\"distribute-a-local-catalog\">Distribute a local catalog</h4> <p>Use <code>model_catalog_json</code> to load the prepared file at startup. A local custom catalog replaces the bundled catalog.</p> <p>Set the gateway alias, catalog <code>slug</code>, and Codex <code>model</code> to <code>company-coding-model</code>. Add these settings before the first TOML table in the Codex configuration you distribute, using the file's actual absolute path:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model = \"company-coding-model\"\nmodel_catalog_json = \"/absolute/path/to/gateway-models.json\"\n</code></pre> <p>Restart the CLI or desktop app after changing the catalog because Codex loads it at startup.</p> <h3 id=\"verify-model-routes\">Verify model routes</h3> <p>For each model, verify the route with a real Responses request and gateway records. A <code>/v1/models</code> response can help discover names but doesn't prove that a model supports the required request and tool behavior.</p> <p>Model routing and tool authorization are separate parts of the rollout. Configure MCP connections, plugin distribution, and their policies separately.</p> <h2 id=\"issue-developer-credentials\">Issue developer credentials</h2> <ol> <li>Issue one scoped gateway credential per developer so you can attribute usage and revoke access individually.</li> <li>Set the approved models, rate limits, budget, expiration, and renewal period for each credential.</li> <li>Deliver credentials through your secret manager or an installed credential helper. Keep upstream provider and gateway administrator credentials off developer machines.</li> <li>If you use a helper, follow the <a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85?anchor=custom-model-providers\">command-backed authentication contract</a> and test token retrieval and refresh before distribution.</li> <li>Tell developers how to renew their credentials and whom to contact for help.</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"test-the-client-and-gateway\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"test-codex-through-the-gateway\">Test Codex through the gateway</h2> <p>Before distributing anything, follow <a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">Use API/provider credentials</a> to configure one isolated test user with the provider block and credential mechanism you plan to distribute.</p> <p>Run the checks below from the same CLI or desktop surface developers will use:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Check</th> <th>Action</th> <th>Passing evidence</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Connection</td> <td>Follow <a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694?anchor=verify-the-connection\">Verify the connection</a>.</td> <td>The expected provider and alias are active, the test prompt succeeds, and gateway logs identify the test user.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Streaming</td> <td>Ask for a short multi-paragraph answer.</td> <td>The gateway forwards SSE events without buffering, text arrives incrementally, and the stream ends with <code>response.completed</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Local tool loop</td> <td>In a disposable folder with read-only permissions, ask Codex to list the top-level files and summarize them.</td> <td>Codex issues a local tool call, returns the result, and produces a final answer without edits.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Follow-up</td> <td>Ask a follow-up in the same thread.</td> <td>The answer uses the prior turn; the gateway accepts replayed input. If WebSocket or incremental transport is enabled, it also preserves <code>previous_response_id</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Errors and attribution</td> <td>Repeat with an intentionally invalid test alias or expired test credential.</td> <td>The client receives a useful routing or authentication error, and valid requests remain attributed to the test user.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>After these checks succeed, direct developers to <a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">Use API/provider credentials</a> to configure and verify their own machine.</p> <h2 id=\"distribute-the-configuration\">Distribute the configuration</h2> <p>To give every machine the same connection path, distribute the gateway base URL, provider ID, approved model alias, and credential mechanism.</p> <h3 id=\"what-to-distribute\">What to distribute</h3> <p>To set provider defaults, distribute this <code>config.toml</code> block through the configuration layer you chose. Use a model recognized by your Codex version, or supply the matching catalog described above. Install your token resolver at the configured command path:</p> <p>Put <code>model</code> and <code>model_provider</code> before the first TOML table. If you set <code>model_catalog_json</code>, keep it there too. TOML treats keys after <code>[model_providers...]</code> as part of that table, not as top-level Codex configuration.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model = \"gpt-6-sol\"\nmodel_provider = \"enterprise-gateway\"\nweb_search = \"disabled\"\n\n[model_providers.enterprise-gateway]\nname = \"Organization Gateway\"\nbase_url = \"https://gateway.example.com/v1\"\nwire_api = \"responses\"\n\n[model_providers.enterprise-gateway.auth]\ncommand = \"/usr/local/bin/fetch-codex-gateway-token\"\nargs = [\"print-token\"]\ntimeout_ms = 30000\nrefresh_interval_ms = 300000\n</code></pre> <p>For a short-lived static test key, remove the auth block and put <code>env_key = \"CODEX_GATEWAY_API_KEY\"</code> inside <code>[model_providers.enterprise-gateway]</code> and set that variable outside TOML. Do not combine <code>env_key</code> with command-backed auth.</p> <h3 id=\"distribute-defaults-and-requirements\">Distribute defaults and requirements</h3> <p>Use <a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76?anchor=configuration-precedence\">Configuration precedence</a> to choose where to distribute defaults. For enforced settings and macOS MDM payloads, see <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=admin-enforced-requirements-requirementstoml\">Managed configuration</a>.</p> <p>For host-wide defaults on macOS or Linux, use <code>/etc/codex/config.toml</code>. On Windows, place <code>config.toml</code> in <code>%ProgramData%\\OpenAI\\Codex\\</code>. Users and profiles can override these defaults. The linked references describe supported requirements and their file locations.</p> <p>Distribute any referenced helper executables and local catalog files separately.</p> <p>To enforce a remote catalog URL, put the complete provider definition in <code>requirements.toml</code> under <code>[model_providers.&lt;id&gt;]</code>. An enforced provider definition replaces the matching provider table from ordinary configuration; include its <code>base_url</code>, authentication settings, and other required fields. Use the <code>model_provider</code> requirement when you also need to enforce provider selection.</p> <p><code>model_catalog_json</code> points to a local JSON file. If you enforce it through <code>requirements.toml</code>, the requirement pins the path; it doesn't distribute the file. Put the catalog at that absolute path before Codex starts.</p> <p>Write resolved absolute Windows paths in TOML. Codex doesn't expand <code>%ProgramData%</code> inside <code>model_catalog_json</code> or provider auth <code>command</code> values. For example, use these paths only if your deployment placed the files there:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model_catalog_json = 'C:\\ProgramData\\OpenAI\\Codex\\models.json'\n\n[model_providers.enterprise-gateway.auth]\ncommand = 'C:\\ProgramData\\OpenAI\\Codex\\fetch-gateway-token.cmd'\nargs = [\"print-token\"]\n</code></pre> <p>A CLI inside WSL reads Linux paths and Linux <code>CODEX_HOME</code>; it doesn't automatically inherit native Windows configuration.</p> <h3 id=\"hand-developers-the-configuration-values\">Hand developers the configuration values</h3> <p>If you do not have managed distribution, give each developer the gateway URL, provider ID, model alias, credential variable or resolver, and any catalog URL or local path. Send them to <a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">Use API/provider credentials</a> to configure and verify their own machine.</p> <p>Manual setup is not an enforcement channel. Project-local <code>.codex/config.toml</code> cannot override sensitive provider or authentication routing keys.</p> <p><a id=\"verify-and-operate-the-rollout\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"verify-from-a-developer-machine\">Verify from a developer machine</h2> <p>To confirm that the distributed settings reached a developer machine:</p> <ol> <li>Restart Codex and confirm the expected provider and model.</li> <li>Run the short test in <a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694?anchor=verify-the-connection\">Use API/provider credentials</a>.</li> <li>Ask one follow-up to confirm continuation, then check the gateway logs for that developer's request.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"troubleshoot-rollout-failures\">Troubleshoot rollout failures</h3> <p>Use the issue to find the configuration, credential, or gateway layer that needs attention:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Issue</th> <th>Remediation</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Expected provider is missing after restart.</td> <td>Inspect the winning configuration layer. User or profile configuration can override system defaults.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Authentication fails for every user.</td> <td>Check gateway authentication and the upstream provider credential; identify which service rejected the request.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Authentication fails for one user.</td> <td>Check that user's gateway credential or token resolver.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Streaming stalls.</td> <td>Inspect gateway buffering and terminal <code>response.completed</code> forwarding.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>A model is missing or uses generic capabilities.</td> <td>For a custom alias, confirm the gateway alias, Codex <code>model</code>, and catalog <code>slug</code> match. Check the <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=use-a-model-catalog-for-custom-names\">catalog</a> path and compatibility with the installed Codex version, then restart Codex.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>A Windows path fails.</td> <td>Use resolved absolute paths. In TOML, use single-quoted strings for Windows paths with single backslashes.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"reuse-an-existing-gateway-deployment\">Reuse an existing gateway deployment</h2> <p>If your organization already uses Claude Code through a gateway, you may be able to reuse the gateway product, network path, logging, and Bedrock access. Add a Codex-facing Responses route, credential, model aliases, and <code>config.toml</code> while retaining the existing working setup. Claude client settings and the <code>/v1/messages</code> contract don't configure Codex.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Existing Claude deployment</th> <th>Codex migration</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Gateway product, DNS, TLS, private networking, logging, redaction, and monitoring</td> <td>Keep these services in place. Add a Codex-facing route that satisfies the <a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">Gateway compatibility requirements</a>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Bedrock account, provider credential, IAM boundary, inference profiles, and credential rotation</td> <td>Keep them only when they authorize the upstream models behind the new Codex aliases. The provider credential remains on the gateway.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Claude <code>/v1/messages</code> route, Bedrock InvokeModel shape, Anthropic headers, and Claude-specific retries or errors</td> <td>Do not reuse these as proof of compatibility. Codex needs <code>POST /v1/responses</code>, Responses streaming, continuation, tool calls, and useful errors.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN</code>, <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code>, or <code>apiKeyHelper</code></td> <td>Codex does not support <code>apiKeyHelper</code>. Issue a scoped Codex gateway credential and configure it with <code>env_key</code> or a Codex command-backed token resolver.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Claude model names, <code>ANTHROPIC_MODEL</code>, <code>ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_*_MODEL</code>, <code>modelOverrides</code>, and Bedrock profile mappings</td> <td>Have your gateway team <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=choose-model-names-and-routes\">choose model names and configure any custom aliases</a>. Use the model name and any <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">model catalog JSON</a> they provide.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Claude <code>settings.json</code>, <code>managed-settings.json</code>, JSON <code>env</code> blocks, <code>plist</code>, or registry payloads</td> <td>Keep the same MDM or configuration-management channel, but distribute Codex <code>config.toml</code> and supported <code>requirements.toml</code> values instead.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>To migrate safely, complete these steps in order:</p> <ol> <li>Inventory the current Claude path: gateway URL, credential source, required headers, model aliases, Bedrock profile mappings, and managed delivery channel.</li> <li>Add a parallel Codex-facing Responses route and Codex model aliases.</li> <li>Issue one scoped Codex credential. If Codex will use a static credential, expose that new credential through <code>env_key</code>; if Claude uses a credential helper, implement and test the Codex command-backed resolver contract.</li> <li>Configure that developer with the <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=what-to-distribute\">provider block</a>. For a managed rollout, translate the payload into the Codex paths and precedence described in <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=distribute-the-configuration\">Roll out a gateway</a>.</li> <li>Run the short connection check on the developer's actual CLI or desktop surface, then run the full streaming, continuation, tool-call, error, logging, and alias-routing checks in <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=test-the-client-and-gateway\">Test Codex through the gateway</a>.</li> <li>After the pilot passes, <a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5?anchor=distribute-the-configuration\">distribute the configuration</a> to the remaining developers.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"related-docs\">Related docs</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">Use API/provider credentials</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Managed configuration</a></li> </ul>"};
